    <description><![CDATA[<h2>GREAT LAKES SURFACE WATER TEMPERATURE</h2><p><b>Gradient key</b><br><img src="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/water_temperature/legend.png" width="600" alt="gradient key"><br>Surface water temperature (°F): cold <b>53°F</b> (deep blue) → <b>61.5°F</b> → warm <b>70°F</b> (red). Lakewide mean this run: <b>62.1°F</b>.</p><p>This entry auto-refreshes from the live overlay (source: NOAA/GLERL CoastWatch GLSEA (Great Lakes Surface Environmental Analysis)).<br/><b>Data time:</b> 2026-09-26 02:50 AM EDT<br/><b>Source version:</b> glsea-Sat-26-Sep-2026-06-50-58-GMT<br/><b>Status:</b> CURRENT DAILY (satellite composite)</p><p>Turn on/off independently of wave and ice layers. Add this file once; new source cycles appear automatically.</p><p><i>Not endorsed by NOAA.</i></p>]]></description>
